<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — Terms & Conditions / EULA startup gate (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual-PARITY reimplementation of the WinForms `Forms/FormTermsAndConditions`
    (FormTermsAndConditions.cs + FormTermsAndConditions.Designer.cs). This is the modal gate the
    operator must Agree to before the program proceeds. Per AAP §0.3.3 this is faithful visual +
    behavioural parity to the currently rendered Windows Forms UI — never a redesign: no new
    colours, no relayout, no UX changes.

    Window shell — mirrors FormTermsAndConditions.Designer.cs exactly:
      ClientSize 1000 x 640        -> Width / Height (SystemDecorations="None" => client == window)
      BackColor Lavender           -> Background="Lavender"  (WinForms Color.Lavender == #FFE6E6FA)
      FormBorderStyle.None         -> SystemDecorations="None"
      TopMost = true               -> Topmost="True"
      (fixed, no control box)      -> CanResize="False"
      StartPosition.CenterScreen   -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner" (shown modally over FormGPS)
      Font Tahoma                  -> FontFamily="Tahoma" (children override FontSize/Weight; the
                                      license box overrides FontFamily to Consolas)

    The CornflowerBlue 10px frame the form painted in OnPaintBackground
    (new Pen(Brushes.CornflowerBlue, 10)) is reproduced declaratively as the root Border's 10px
    BorderBrush="CornflowerBlue" edge. The literal Lavender / CornflowerBlue / Black colours come
    straight from the WinForms source and intentionally take precedence over App.axaml's day/night
    theme brushes for this dialog (1:1 parity, and theme-light text would be illegible on the fixed
    light background) — exactly as the sibling FormDialogView / FormInputDialogView do. App.axaml's
    FluentTheme still supplies the default Button / TextBox / ScrollBar control templates.

    Wiring contract — the partner code-behind (FormTermsAndConditionsView.axaml.cs) owns behaviour:
      * No DataContext / no x:DataType / no {Binding}: a code-behind dialog like the sibling
        FormYesView / FormInputDialogView. The x:Name'd controls below are the entire integration
        surface and MUST keep these names to match the generated fields the code-behind references:
        pictureBoxWarning, labelTermsAndConditions, labelVersion, labelVersionActual, labelTerms,
        textBoxLicense, buttonGitHub, buttonDiscourse, buttonYouTube, labelDisagree, labelAgree.
      * Form_About_Load parity: the code-behind assigns the translated captions at runtime
        (labelTermsAndConditions=gStr.gsTermsConditions, labelVersion=gStr.gsVersion+":",
        labelTerms=gStr.gsTerms, labelAgree=gStr.gsAgree, labelDisagree=gStr.gsDisagree,
        buttonGitHub=gStr.gsCheckForUpdates, buttonDiscourse=gStr.gsDiscourseForum,
        buttonYouTube=gStr.gsYouTubeTutorials) and labelVersionActual=Program.SemVer. The Text
        values set below are the original English design-time strings; the textBoxLicense Apache 2.0
        text is the resx default and is NOT reassigned at runtime, so it is carried here verbatim.
      * labelAgree carried DialogResult.OK and labelDisagree DialogResult.Cancel; the code-behind
        routes their Click to close with the corresponding result (the operator must Agree to
        proceed). The three link buttons' Click open GitHub / Discourse / YouTube via the OS browser
        (Process.Start), reproducing buttonGitHub/Discourse/YouTube_Click.

    Layout: the WinForms form used absolute Location/Size for all 11 controls, so a Canvas inside the
    10px frame is the faithful 1:1 analog. Every Canvas.Left/Canvas.Top below is the WinForms
    Location minus the 10px frame inset (so each control keeps its original on-screen position); the
    inner content area is therefore 980 x 620. Fonts use the WinForms point size x 96/72 = device
    independent pixels (e.g. 18pt -> 24, 14pt -> 18.667, 12pt -> 16, 11pt -> 14.667).

    Button glyphs are served from the GPS assembly (assembly name "AgOpenGPS") via avares:// URIs —
    the same btnImages/ assets the sibling GPS Avalonia views consume (all confirmed 64 x 64).
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.FormTermsAndConditionsView"
        Title="AgOpenGPS"
        Width="1000"
        Height="640"
        Background="{DynamicResource AogLegacyLavenderBrush}"
        SystemDecorations="None"
        CanResize="False"
        Topmost="True"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        FontFamily="Tahoma">

    <!--
        Flat image-over-text buttons reproduce the WinForms FlatStyle.Flat +
        FlatAppearance.BorderSize = 0 + BackColor = Transparent. All five buttons (the three link
        buttons and Agree / Disagree) set FlatAppearance.MouseOverBackColor = CornflowerBlue, so the
        :pointerover / :pressed template overrides fill the content presenter CornflowerBlue on hover
        / press; the rest state is fully transparent over the Lavender body.
    -->
    <Window.Styles>
        <Style Selector="Button.linkButton">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.linkButton:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="CornflowerBlue" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="CornflowerBlue" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.linkButton:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="CornflowerBlue" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="CornflowerBlue" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <!--
        RootBorder == the 10px CornflowerBlue frame painted in OnPaintBackground; its Lavender
        Background fills the interior (WinForms BackColor). The Canvas reproduces the absolute
        WinForms layout; its origin is the inner top-left (window 10,10), so every child coordinate
        is the WinForms Location minus 10. Inner content area = 980 x 620.
    -->
    <Border BorderThickness="10"
            BorderBrush="CornflowerBlue"
            Background="Lavender">

        <Canvas Width="980" Height="620">

            <!-- pictureBoxWarning: WinForms PictureBox (300,20) 64x64, Image Resources.Warning. -->
            <Image x:Name="pictureBoxWarning"
                   Canvas.Left="290"
                   Canvas.Top="10"
                   Width="64"
                   Height="64"
                   Stretch="Uniform"
                   Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/Warning.png" />

            <!-- labelTermsAndConditions: WinForms Label (380,30) 580x45, Tahoma 18 Bold, MiddleLeft.
                 The transparent Border supplies the fixed box + vertical centring (TextBlock has no
                 vertical text alignment); runtime text = gStr.gsTermsConditions. -->
            <Border Canvas.Left="370" Canvas.Top="20" Width="580" Height="45" Background="Transparent">
                <TextBlock x:Name="labelTermsAndConditions"
                           Text="Terms and Conditions"
                           FontSize="24"
                           FontWeight="Bold"
                           Foreground="Black"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                           VerticalAlignment="Center"
                           TextAlignment="Left" />
            </Border>

            <!-- labelVersion: WinForms Label (380,75) 120x25, Tahoma 11, MiddleRight. -->
            <Border Canvas.Left="370" Canvas.Top="65" Width="120" Height="25" Background="Transparent">
                <TextBlock x:Name="labelVersion"
                           Text="Version:"
                           FontSize="14.667"
                           Foreground="Black"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                           VerticalAlignment="Center"
                           TextAlignment="Right" />
            </Border>

            <!-- labelVersionActual: WinForms Label (505,75) 350x25, Tahoma 11, MiddleLeft. Runtime
                 text = Program.SemVer; "x.y.z" is the designer placeholder. -->
            <Border Canvas.Left="495" Canvas.Top="65" Width="350" Height="25" Background="Transparent">
                <TextBlock x:Name="labelVersionActual"
                           Text="x.y.z"
                           FontSize="14.667"
                           Foreground="Black"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                           VerticalAlignment="Center"
                           TextAlignment="Left" />
            </Border>

            <!-- labelTerms: WinForms Label (180,135) 780x230, Tahoma 14 Bold, MiddleCenter. Runtime
                 text = gStr.gsTerms; the English design-time disclaimer is carried below verbatim. -->
            <Border Canvas.Left="170" Canvas.Top="125" Width="780" Height="230" Background="Transparent">
                <TextBlock x:Name="labelTerms"
                           FontSize="18.667"
                           FontWeight="Bold"
                           Foreground="Black"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                           VerticalAlignment="Center"
                           TextAlignment="Center"
                           TextWrapping="Wrap"
                           xml:space="preserve"><TextBlock.Text>AgOpenGPS is strictly educational software to learn about guidance systems, GPS sentences, and theoretical application of machine control.

It is in no way to be used on real equipment in any circumstance. A simulator is provided to allow the student to safely experience machine guidance.

There are no safety systems in the software and none are implied.

USE AT OWN RISK.
</TextBlock.Text></TextBlock>
            </Border>

            <!-- textBoxLicense: WinForms TextBox (180,385) 780x135, Consolas 12, Multiline, ReadOnly,
                 ScrollBars=Vertical (WordWrap on), BackColor White, BorderStyle FixedSingle. The
                 Apache 2.0 text is the resx default and is NOT reassigned at runtime, so it is
                 carried here verbatim. -->
            <TextBox x:Name="textBoxLicense"
                     AutomationProperties.Name="License text"
                     Canvas.Left="170"
                     Canvas.Top="375"
                     Width="780"
                     Height="135"
                     FontFamily="Consolas"
                     FontSize="16"
                     AcceptsReturn="True"
                     IsReadOnly="True"
                     TextWrapping="Wrap"
                     Background="White"
                     Foreground="Black"
                     BorderBrush="Gray"
                     BorderThickness="1"
                     ScrollViewer.VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Visible"
                     ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                     xml:space="preserve"><TextBox.Text>                                 Apache License
                           Version 2.0, January 2004
                        http://www.apache.org/licenses/

